From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:46:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: Windows.Gaming.Input finds the title's controller (patch
 0477)

A game that reads its controller through Windows.Gaming.Input (Unity's,
as in Deep Rock Galactic Survivor) found none on the console: Wine's
providers come from the HID stack in winedevice.exe, which a title
cannot start, while XInput saw the title's controller.

Patch 0477 adds a provider that reads the controller through xinput's
Unix library, as xinput does: a Gamepad and a RawGameController, the
Xbox controller XInput reports (045e:028e), whose rumble and buzz reach
the DualSense's motors. The monitor thread looks for it before handing
out the factories, then four times a second, so it goes and comes back
with the controller. Only xinput mode publishes the controller; outside
a title nothing changes.

Tested on the PC's Wine with the title's side stood in for, 64- and
32-bit: the gamepad is there at the first query; buttons, d-pad, sticks
and triggers read as XInput gives them; the RawGameController's ids,
counts, reading and name; vibration reaches the title and reads back;
GamepadRemoved and GamepadAdded when the controller goes and returns.
Without a title no gamepad appears.
