+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:45:00 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] windows.gaming.input: The PS5 title's controller as a gamepad.
+
+Windows.Gaming.Input finds controllers through the HID stack, which runs
+in winedevice.exe; a PS5 title cannot start that process, so on the
+console a game that reads its controller this way (Unity's, as in Deep
+Rock Galactic Survivor) found none, while XInput saw the title's.
+
+In xinput mode the title keeps its controller's state where xinput's
+Unix library reads it (patch 0470). A provider reads it the same way:
+the game finds the Xbox controller XInput reports, 045e:028e, as a
+Gamepad and a RawGameController, with the six axes, ten buttons and
+switch of an Xbox controller's HID collection, in the order gamepad.c
+reads them. Its rumble and buzz reach the DualSense's two motors.
+
+The monitor thread looks for the title's controller before it hands
+out the factories, so a game that asks for the gamepads at once finds
+it, and then four times a second: the provider goes when the controller
+disconnects, with GamepadRemoved, and a new one comes when it connects
+again. Anywhere but in a title the library finds no title, the thread
+waits as before, and nothing changes.
